# The archived Figma-Make wireframes are a BUILD ARTIFACT of another tool (minified Tailwind in a single
# `<style>` block, one enormous `:root` token declaration, hand-authored-looking markup that is generated).
# They are feature 001's visual contract, and reformatting them reflows every line — which both destroys the
# archive's fidelity to what Figma exported and buries the colour/label-class edits the design system actually
# needs in a whole-file rewrite. Their design tokens and label pairings are guarded by measurement instead:
# `packages/tools/test-utils/src/__tests__/mockupContrast.test.ts`. The README beside them is NOT ignored.
docs/mockups/screens
docs/mockups/_assets

# The generated OpenAPI documents. They are DERIVED output written by `@kitchensink/contract-gen`
# (CODING_STANDARDS §15.2) and guarded by CI's regenerate-and-diff, so any reformatting here — even a
# harmless one — reads as contract drift and reds that gate until the generator is re-run. Prettier happens
# to leave today's output byte-identical; this entry is what stops a future prettier release from turning
# that coincidence into a permanently-failing check nobody can explain.
packages/schemas/*/openapi.yaml

# The staged Python Lambda asset — ~3,000 files of pip output (third-party Python, licences, model cards)
# rewritten by `npm run bundle:lambda`. It is gitignored build output that this repository did not author,
# and reformatting a dependency's own README changes nothing anyone reads while making `format:check` walk
# 91 MB. See ADR-0025.
packages/services/ingredient-parser/build

# The generated component + design-token documentation. DERIVED output written by
# `@kitchensink/docgen-components` and guarded by regenerate-and-diff, exactly like the OpenAPI documents
# above and for the identical reason: the guard compares BYTES, and `lint-staged` runs `prettier --write` on
# every staged `*.json`, so without this entry a commit reformats the artifact and the gate reds on drift
# that is not drift. Prettier happens to leave today's output nearly identical; the point is that it must not
# be able to touch it at all.
docs/generated/components
docs/generated/design

